Attempting to save over an existing file by using "save as" should prompt for
for confirmation via the minibuffer. If the prompt is denied then the save
should not take place.

-- config --
path: tests/data/config/without-fsys.toml
-- file-a.txt --
a
-- file-b.txt --
b
-- actions --
# attempt to save
type: :w a.txt\n
# should be presented with the minibuffer asking for confirmation
type: n\n
-- buffer-list --
1      a.txt
2    * b.txt
-- expected-windows --
2
-- expected-buffer-1 --
a
-- expected-buffer-2 --
b
